+   * 10 ms after the port reset was cleared; the rp2 controller retried,
+   * every retry timed out, the 0.21 hcd failed the transfer on the first
+   * timeout, and the stack abandoned the device (no retry of a failed
+   * enumeration).  An event log showed it: seven RX timeouts in 120 us,
+   * four FAILED, then a STALL on the next device.  0.20 waited longer and
+   * tolerated timeouts, and the same devices enumerate under it; so did
+   * 0.21 whenever a debug print stretched this gap.  Ten devices at 90 ms
+   * each is under a second of boot; a device still not ready after 100 ms
+   * is a device to replug.  (2026-09-01, ports/rp2/usbh.patch) */
+  ENUM_RESET_RECOVERY_DELAY_MS       = 100, // T(RSTRCY) minimum 10 ms for reset recovery - PC3: 100
   ENUM_SET_ADDRESS_RECOVERY_DELAY_MS = 2,   // USB 2.0 Spec 9.2.6.3 min is 2 ms
 };
 
